refuse tag stencil: an action inside a tag, outside an attribute value, is not supported
refuse template call stencil: a template call outside element text is not supported
refuse predefined stencil: a predefined escaper (html or urlquery) in an action is not supported
refuse regexp stencil: an action in a JavaScript regular expression is not supported
refuse template literal stencil: a template literal in a <script> is not supported
refuse unquoted quote stencil: a quote, <, = or backtick in an unquoted attribute value is not supported
refuse srcset stencil: an action in a srcset attribute is not supported
refuse meta stencil: an action in a meta tag is not supported
refuse end in context stencil: t: the template ends inside an HTML context
refuse script end in string stencil: <script, </script or <!-- inside a JavaScript string is not supported
refuse if crosses stencil: an if block crosses an HTML context boundary
if same context <p>x</p>
